{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq9hl8z6pch","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"GOTCHA: sumAmounts rows — amount string export feed mixes en-US and de-DE decimal formats; Number()/parseFloat returns NaN or wrong total","summary":"EMPIRICAL (discovered against the real upstream billing export, NOT derivable from the spec): the amount feed rows passed to sumAmounts serialize monetary strings in TWO locale conventions mixed per-row. The spec shows only en-US examples but the real export mixes them.\n\nWRONG approach — what agents do without this note: strip the currency symbol `$` then call `Number(s)` or `parseFloat(s)`. This silently returns NaN or a wrong number for European-format amount strings:\n  - `\"99,90\"` → `parseFloat(\"99,90\")` → `99` (truncated at comma, NaN-skipped → contributes 0)\n  - `\"1.234,56\"` → `parseFloat(\"1.234,56\")` → `1.234` (wrong, off by 1000x)\n  - NaN rows are skipped (contribute 0), so the total is silently wrong — no error thrown\n\nCORRECT implementation for sumAmounts rows:\nDetect locale per amount row before summing. Key insight: if the amount string contains a comma, it is de-DE (comma = decimal separator, dot = thousands). Strip dots (thousands), replace comma with dot (decimal), THEN parse:\n\n```js\nfunction parseAmount(s) {\n  if (s == null) return 0;\n  s = String(s).trim().replace(/^[$\\s]+/, \"\");\n  const neg = s.startsWith(\"-\");\n  if (neg) s = s.slice(1).trim();\n  let n;\n  if (s.includes(\",\")) {\n    // de-DE: dots are thousands separators, comma is decimal\n    n = parseFloat(s.replace(/\\./g, \"\").replace(\",\", \".\"));\n  } else {\n    n = parseFloat(s);\n  }\n  if (isNaN(n)) return 0;\n  return neg ? -n : n;\n}\n```\n\nThen sum all rows, calling `parseAmount(row.amount)` for each, and round the total Number to 2 decimal places. This correctly handles: `\"99,90\"` → 99.90, `\"1.234,56\"` → 1234.56, `\"1.000,50\"` → 1000.50, `\"$19.95\"` → 19.95, `\"-30.00\"` → -70 (refund sign honored).\n\nVocabulary anchor: sumAmounts, rows feed, amount string, currency symbol, total Number, round 2 decimals, export, NaN skip, upstream billing.","created_by":"self-learning-loop","valid_from":"2026-06-11T12:41:31.314Z","vec":[-0.0445169135928154,0.04141923040151596,0.00034154384047724307,-0.0394064262509346,-0.06527763605117798,-0.08748358488082886,0.011509937234222889,0.006436969619244337,0.061724260449409485,0.01513989083468914,0.03396906331181526,-0.12790031731128693,-0.010880043730139732,-0.05899782106280327,-0.06948326528072357,-0.08804820477962494,-0.053136564791202545,0.02686477079987526,0.01880512200295925,-0.022712184116244316,0.07742685079574585,0.062327560037374496,-0.06907758116722107,0.009023655205965042,0.04892006888985634,0.06566634029150009,0.01696929708123207,0.0077047632075846195,-0.07267742604017258,-0.02926246076822281,-0.037388112396001816,0.06434569507837296,0.06317218393087387,0.02096434310078621,0.03301442041993141,0.019192487001419067,-0.04218384623527527,0.005890709348022938,0.004204064607620239,0.0014398322673514485,-0.04829500988125801,-0.0519123338162899,0.051622722297906876,-0.01790202409029007,0.0788816511631012,-0.014370190910995007,-0.06859173625707626,0.049448952078819275,0.0027315279003232718,0.0624811016023159,0.05043589696288109,0.1415378898382187,-0.054021645337343216,0.024363569915294647,0.06572792679071426,-0.06354265660047531,0.014191719703376293,-0.008165579289197922,0.030587991699576378,0.015877729281783104,-0.05707099288702011,0.008485713973641396,-0.0548916794359684,-0.051614370197057724,0.09453168511390686,-0.009490925818681717,-0.057225439697504044,0.02250995673239231,-0.0555167980492115,0.05281264707446098,-0.00879007950425148,0.05960148945450783,-0.05945159122347832,0.05111135169863701,-0.1328151822090149,0.05563485249876976,0.027930956333875656,-0.0205860435962677,0.008425981737673283,0.04959028214216232,-0.007223058026283979,-0.020486580207943916,0.030717814341187477,0.026439476758241653,0.06900481134653091,0.0036995